  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1253 PM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nRain potential Thursday night continues to look minimal, with\nprobability guidance showing a small 10-20% chance of any rain \n(0.01\") just brushing parts of Kewaunee, Calumet, and Manitowoc \ncounties. Deterministic models are less enthused and show any rain\nstaying south/east. Kept some small PoPs in the far southeast \nforecast area which only amounts to sprinkles. While the precip \nfrom this system remains elsewhere, northeast WI is in close \nenough proximity to see increased winds due to a tightening \npressure gradient. From Thursday afternoon through Friday morning,\nnortheast to north winds will gust to around 30 mph across the \nFox Valley and east-central WI.\n\nOver the course of the weekend, both a northern and southern\nstream low pressure system move across North America. The northern\nlow tracks across central Canada, with a trailing cold front which\ncrosses WI on Saturday night into Sunday morning. The southern \nlow tracks across the central Plains and into the Ohio River \nValley, and could bring minor precip/rain to the southeast\nforecast area. There is a small (10-20%) chance for minor snow/mixed\nprecip early Saturday morning in association with some weak WAA. \nOtherwise, the best chance for any precipitation will be \nassociated with the cold front Sunday morning and afternoon. \n\nPotential for a tenth of an inch of rain ranges from 20-40%,\nhighest across the Fox Valley and east-central WI. While\ntemperature profiles there support rain, central and northern WI\nare colder and would support snow. There is a 20-60% chance for a\ntenth of an inch of snow in north- central WI, highest in Vilas\nCounty. With a 20% chance for 0.5\" only in northern Vilas County.\nNormally, this would be low impact, but there could be extra \ntravelers on the road after the holiday weekend. Any snow could \ncreated slippery spots, so drivers should use extra caution. \n\nTemperatures...Normal high temps for late November range from\nabout 35 to 40 degrees, with normal lows in the upper teens and\nlow 20s. While daily readings will fluctuate a little bit, temps\nare forecast to remain at or above normal for the next week.\nHowever, it may seem cooler since it has been well above normal\nfor much of November.",
